# Page Chrome

Do **not** put a boxed/gradient `PageHero` (or a giant centered header card) on new or rebuilt pages. That Dec 2025 pattern is retired.

## Studios (default for any area with more than one route)

Follow `rules/STUDIO_PAGE_BUILDING_RULES.md`. Layout owns chrome:

```
StudioProvider
  AreaBar          ← outside <main>, full-width on mobile
  <main>           ← padding + --content-px
    {children}     ← no second page header
```

- Register the prefix in `STUDIO_ROUTE_PREFIXES` (`src/lib/navigation/page-classifications.ts`)
- Pages inside a studio do **not** add `PageHero`, `PageHeader`, or a custom title banner
- Admin is a studio (`/admin`). `AdminAreaBar` uses the real `AreaBar`. Default is title-only. Pages push tabs with `useAdminStudioChrome` only for in-page views that are not already sidebar destinations.

## Standalone pages (one-off routes with no AreaBar)

Slim left-aligned title only. Use `PageHero` (now a title row, not a card) or a plain `h1`.

```tsx
<Container size="xl">
  <Stack gap="lg">
    <PageHero title="Page title" subtitle="One line, optional">
      <Button size="sm">Primary action</Button>
    </PageHero>
    {/* content */}
  </Stack>
</Container>
```

## Never

- Gradient-bordered / padded hero cards as page headers
- Centered `text-4xl`/`text-5xl` page titles
- `PageHero` inside a studio layout
- Copying templates from old `PAGE_BUILDING_RULES` that say “PageHero is required”
